<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander II of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Alexander II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> was emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> from 1855 to 1881, known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Liberator. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-reforms-russia">Great Reforms</a> included the emancipation of the serfs in 1861, together with changes to local government, the courts and the army. He was assassinated by revolutionaries in 1881.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia.jpg" alt="Alexander II of Russia" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to W. &amp; D. Downey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zar_Alexander_II_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
